The full legal code is referenced by URL rather than copied here, which is how
Creative Commons intends its licences to be applied. The URL above is authoritative;
nothing in this file modifies it.

IN SHORT, AND WITHOUT REPLACING THE LICENCE ITSELF

  You may share and adapt this content, including commercially, provided you give
  appropriate credit and license your adaptations under the same terms.

WHY SHARE-ALIKE IS HERE AND NOT ON THE CODE

  Per ADR-0004. The code is first-party infrastructure that nobody wants in isolation.
  This directory is the product, and it is the part a competitor would lift. Share-alike
  is on it for that reason: adaptations stay open. The code carries Apache-2.0 instead,
  because its patent grant is worth more there than copyleft would be.

WHAT THIS LICENCE DOES NOT REACH

  A rule pack authored by a third party is not a derivative work of this corpus merely
  because Fathom can load both. A workspace is the user's own document. See the root
  LICENSE.

A WARNING THAT IS NOT A LICENCE TERM

  Under invariant 10, no entry here is content until a named human has reviewed it and
  is recorded in its `reviewed_by` field. Entries still carrying the `<named human>`
  placeholder have NOT been verified against real equipment. They are licensed to you
  all the same; they are not warranted, and Section 5 of the licence disclaims exactly
  this. Check the field before you rely on an entry.
